Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Geared Step Motor Considerations", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9354887736332293`*^9, 3.935488782776742*^9}, {
  3.935489878019535*^9, 3.935489883954569*^9}, {3.935498260987459*^9, 
  3.935498262891034*^9}, {3.9356058911259117`*^9, 3.9356058924940643`*^9}, {
  3.9356587358752127`*^9, 
  3.935658743186392*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1477ffb5-7dba-4a22-b3f2-\
9f77abdd4970"],

Cell["\<\
The geared step motor Model 17HS13-0404S-PG5 is manufactured by many \
companies. It has a nominal ratio between the input step motor and output \
planetary gear box of 5:1. This means that if the step motor shaft (internal \
to the unit) rotates by 5 revs then the  gear box output shaft rotates by 1 \
rev. 
However, this is the nominal value. The actual value is:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93560593406254*^9, 3.9356060165668097`*^9}, {
  3.935606148671761*^9, 
  3.935606311359915*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e0a79419-89b6-4daf-a01f-\
23b108956518"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  ButtonBox["\<\"\[GraySquare]\"\>",
   Appearance->"Frameless",
   ButtonFunction:>(SelectionMove[
      EvaluationCell[], All, TextLine]; SelectionEvaluate[
      EvaluationNotebook[]]),
   Evaluator->Automatic,
   Method->"Preemptive"], ";", "  ", 
  RowBox[{"gearRatio", "=", 
   RowBox[{"5.", "+", 
    RowBox[{"2", "/", "11"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.935606089625012*^9, 3.93560610119973*^9}, 
   3.935606335328198*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[99]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4f985b6d-bd23-4484-96ea-11c11cba037c"],

Cell[BoxData["5.181818181818182`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.935606104820674*^9, 3.935606340563581*^9, 
  3.950017328651019*^9, 3.950017499289136*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[99]=",ExpressionUUID->"389c7e56-0ab5-4457-8842-2e7b0d3818d6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["We will need this value in the code below.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.935606350878632*^9, 
  3.935606369856246*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"63fe6600-5c49-4a15-955e-\
4a379d869c54"],

Cell["\<\
The TinkerForge Silent Stepper Bricklet can drive a maximum current per phase \
of 1.6 A and a minimum voltage of 8 V and maximum of 46 V. We use 1.5 A and \
12 V here. 
Like almost all step motors the one used here has 200 macro-steps per rev of \
the step motor before the gear box. The Silent Stepper Bricklet can \
interpolate between steps. These interpolated steps are often called \
micro-steps. The Silent Stepper Bricklet can produce 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, \
128 or 256 micro-steps per macro step. So for example if we select 256 \
micro-step interpolation then we get 256 x 200 = 51,200 micro-steps per rev \
of the step motor before the gear box.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.935489009219194*^9, 3.935489067258821*^9}, {
   3.935489797795402*^9, 3.935489863995572*^9}, {3.9354898976275177`*^9, 
   3.935489901810812*^9}, {3.935489964122962*^9, 3.9354902110177*^9}, 
   3.935605907398322*^9, {3.93565683465639*^9, 3.935656835185615*^9}, {
   3.935656876248979*^9, 3.935656893247882*^9}, {3.935657037982871*^9, 
   3.935657048952757*^9}, 3.935657085154603*^9, {3.935657187590828*^9, 
   3.935657197591353*^9}, {3.9356577710266943`*^9, 
   3.935657783947494*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9ec50f1c-01d6-4714-a126-\
c00e30af0646"],

Cell["\<\
So the total number of micro-steps to produce 1 rev of the gear box output \
shaft is:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9356571043202677`*^9, 3.935657119038238*^9}, {
  3.935658812034917*^9, 
  3.935658842809589*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e10ceb8b-bfb3-4180-86af-\
300a94d76e7b"],

