Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Check IMU Angle", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.935658938594837*^9, 3.935658943587535*^9}, {
  3.935662847555195*^9, 
  3.935662858792725*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d33eb3e6-be11-4c2d-8cca-\
a35bdd82f4c2"],

Cell["\<\
Note that the imu returns angle with respect to the earth. It can only be \
considered to measure shaft angle if the geared step motor body remains fixed \
in space. So during the experiment below you need to make sure that the \
geared step motor shaft is vertical and the body does no move as its shaft \
rotates.
Manually rotate the step motor body (not just the shaft) until you get an \
angle of just below 0.0 (e.g., between 359.5 and 0.0 deg). Rerun this code \
until you get the angle just below 0.0:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.935664497430624*^9, 3.9356645310384398`*^9}, {
  3.9356725927323513`*^9, 3.935672942308552*^9}, {3.9356730815302343`*^9, 
  3.935673151955711*^9}, {3.9356732303456573`*^9, 3.935673231162921*^9}, {
  3.95002068813811*^9, 3.95002069840939*^9}, {3.95002073732164*^9, 
  3.9500207386251717`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3cebd63f-091e-4fa8-8846-\
025db64ccd20"],

